Here are a few ways to write a JavaScript function that removes duplicates from an array, depending on whether you need to preserve the original order or not.

### 1. Using `Set` (Recommended for simplicity and performance)

The `Set` object lets you store unique values of any type. This is the most modern and concise way to remove duplicates.

```javascript
/**
 * Removes duplicate elements from an array, preserving the order of first appearance.
 * @param {Array<any>} arr The input array which may contain duplicates.
 * @returns {Array<any>} A new array with duplicates removed.
 */
function removeDuplicatesUsingSet(arr) {
  // Create a new Set from the array, which automatically handles uniqueness,
  // and then convert it back to an array using the spread operator.
  return [...new Set(arr)];
}

// Example Usage:
